#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (First Indian Public Appearance):* Assuming it was Champaran (1917). Gandhi's first major public appearance was at the *opening of Banaras Hindu University (BHU) in February 1916*.
  2. *Trap 2 (Early Satyagraha Order):* Placing Kheda before Ahmedabad. The chronological order is *Champaran (1917) $arrow.r$ Ahmedabad (Feb–Mar 1918) $arrow.r$ Kheda (Mar–Jun 1918)*.
  3. *Trap 3 (Knighthood vs Kaiser-i-Hind):* Confusing awards renounced. *Rabindranath Tagore* renounced his *Knighthood* post-Jallianwala Bagh; *Gandhi* returned his *Kaiser-i-Hind* gold medal in 1920.
  4. *Trap 4 (Round Table Attendance):* Assuming Congress attended all RTCs. Congress attended *only the Second RTC (1931)*, where Gandhi was the sole representative.
  5. *Trap 5 (Poona Pact Signatories):* Believing Gandhi personally signed the Poona Pact. Gandhi was fasting; *Madan Mohan Malaviya* signed on behalf of caste Hindus, and *Dr. B.R. Ambedkar* signed for the Depressed Classes.
  6. *Trap 6 (Independence Day Date in 1930):* Confusing 15 August with 26 January. Under the Lahore Congress resolution, *26 January 1930* was celebrated as the First Independence Day.
  7. *Trap 7 (Direct Action Day Catalyst):* Direct Action Day was called on *16 August 1946* by the Muslim League post-Cabinet Mission breakdown, NOT during the 1942 Quit India Movement!
]

